IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-terms`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-amount`

-- Old Age Security Act, PART III, sections 21 and 21.1: the allowance for a survivor aged 60 to 64, and the case in
-- which it is not payable because the survivor has been convicted of killing the deceased. Piece oa2.
--
-- As in section 19, the facts about one survivor and one month are a record, each paragraph is a rule over it, and one
-- rule puts them together. The age reading is the one set out at the head of oa2-part3-spouse-allowance (fork
-- F-AGE-1): a month is paid when the survivor is 60 to 64 on the last day of the month before it, which is what
-- subsections 21(6) and 21(8) say in words (begins the month after the survivor attains 60; ends on the expiration of
-- the month in which the survivor attains 65).

§ `Part III -- Monthly Allowances`

§§ `Allowance payable to a survivor, section 21`

DECLARE `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month` HAS
    `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the person became a survivor` IS A DATE
    `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouses or common-law partners made a joint application for an allowance under section 19 before the pensioner's death for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and the payment period is one in respect of which it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS A DATE
    `the person was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the person became a survivor` IS A DATE
    `the month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force` IS A DATE
    `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the person left Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Immigration and Refugee Protection Act (no piece; a plain input)
    `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Regulations section 22.1 (piece oa3)
    `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS A MAYBE `Sentence of imprisonment`
    `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the month in which the person is released` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the person dies` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- (1) "an allowance may be paid to a survivor who": "survivor" is the keel's section 2 definition: a person whose
-- spouse or common-law partner has died and who has not thereafter become the spouse or common-law partner of another.
-- src:573 | 21 (1) Subject to this Act and the regulations, for each month in any payment period, an allowance may be paid to a survivor who
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(1) survivor (src:573)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1): the person is a survivor` facts MEANS
    `the person is a survivor` (facts's `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died`) (facts's `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person`)

-- (1)(a) "has attained sixty years of age but has not attained sixty-five years of age" (fork F-AGE-1).
-- src:574 | (a) has attained sixty years of age but has not attained sixty-five years of age; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(1)(a) (src:574)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1)(a): the survivor is at least sixty and under sixty-five` month facts MEANS
        age AT LEAST 60
    AND age LESS THAN 65
    WHERE
        age MEANS `the age in complete years on` (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 1) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` month)) `of a person born on` (facts's `the person's date of birth`)

-- (1)(b) "has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which their application
-- is approved for an aggregate period of at least ten years and, where that aggregate period is less than twenty
-- years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which their application is approved."
-- src:575 | (b) has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which their application is approved for an aggregate period of at least ten years and, where that aggregate period is less than twenty years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which their application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(1)(b) (src:575)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1)(b): the survivor has the required residence in Canada` facts MEANS
    aggregate AT LEAST 10
    AND (   aggregate AT LEAST 20
         OR facts's `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved`)
    WHERE
        aggregate MEANS facts's `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years`

-- (2) "A survivor is eligible for an allowance under this section only if (a) on the day preceding the day on which
-- their application for an allowance is approved they are a Canadian citizen or, if not, are legally resident in
-- Canada; or (b) on the day preceding the day they ceased to reside in Canada they were a Canadian citizen or, if
-- not, were legally resident in Canada." (3) the regulations on the meaning of legal residence are piece oa3's.
-- src:577 | (2) A survivor is eligible for an allowance under this section only if
-- src:578 | (a) on the day preceding the day on which their application for an allowance is approved they are a Canadian citizen or, if not, are legally resident in Canada; or
-- src:579 | (b) on the day preceding the day they ceased to reside in Canada they were a Canadian citizen or, if not, were legally resident in Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(2) (src:577-579)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(2): the survivor's residence in Canada is or was legal` facts MEANS
        (   facts's `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen`
         OR facts's `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada`)
    OR  (   facts's `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen`
         OR facts's `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada`)

-- (4) "Subject to subsections (5) and (5.1), no allowance may be paid to a survivor under this section in any payment
-- period unless the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of that payment period and payment
-- of the allowance has been approved under this Part."
-- (5) "Where the spouses or the common-law partners had, before the death of the pensioner, made a joint application
-- for the allowance under section 19 for months in the payment period of the pensioner's death or the following
-- payment period, no application is required to be made by the pensioner's survivor under subsection (4) in respect of
-- the payment of an allowance under this section for months in the payment period in respect of which the joint
-- application was made." (11) subsection (10) applies to those months after the pensioner's death. (5.1) "The Minister
-- may waive the requirement referred to in subsection (4) for an application".
-- src:583 | (4) Subject to subsections (5) and (5.1), no allowance may be paid to a survivor under this section in any payment period unless the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of that payment period and payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part.
-- src:584 | Exception to application requirement
-- src:585 | (5) Where the spouses or the common-law partners had, before the death of the pensioner, made a joint application for the allowance under section 19 for months in the payment period of the pensioner’s death or the following payment period, no application is required to be made by the pensioner’s survivor under subsection (4) in respect of the payment of an allowance under this section for months in the payment period in respect of which the joint application was made.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(4), s 21(5) (src:583-585)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(4): the requirement for an application and approval is met for the payment period` facts MEANS
        (   facts's `the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of the payment period`
         OR facts's `the spouses or common-law partners made a joint application for an allowance under section 19 before the pensioner's death for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and the payment period is one in respect of which it was made`
         OR facts's `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)`)
    AND facts's `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part`

-- src:587 | (5.1) The Minister may waive the requirement referred to in subsection (4) for an application for payment of an allowance for any month or months in a payment period if an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of any payment period before that payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(5.1) (src:587)
GIVEN `an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of a payment period before the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(5.1): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` `an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of a payment period before the payment period` MEANS
    `an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of a payment period before the payment period`

-- (5.2) and (5.3): notice not later than fifteen days before the month.
-- src:589 | (5.2) Where the requirement for an application for payment of an allowance for any month or months in a payment period has been waived under subsection (5.1) and an application is required for payment of an allowance for any subsequent month or months in that payment period, the Minister shall, not later than fifteen days before that subsequent month or the first of those subsequent months, notify the survivor in writing that an application is required.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(5.2) (src:589)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1) for a month or months in the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application is required for payment of an allowance for a subsequent month or months in that payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(5.2): the Minister must notify the survivor in writing that an application is required` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1) for a month or months in the payment period` `an application is required for payment of an allowance for a subsequent month or months in that payment period` MEANS
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1) for a month or months in the payment period` AND `an application is required for payment of an allowance for a subsequent month or months in that payment period`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(5.2) "not later than fifteen days before" (src:589)
GIVEN `the first of the subsequent months for which an application is required` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(5.2): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the subsequent months for which an application is required` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in days` 15) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` `the first of the subsequent months for which an application is required`)

-- src:591 | (5.3) Notwithstanding that the requirement for an application for payment of an allowance for any month or months has been waived under subsection (5.1), the Minister may require that the survivor make such an application for that month or for any of those months, and in such a case, the Minister shall, not later than fifteen days before that month or the first of those months, notify the survivor in writing that an application is required.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(5.3) (src:591)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires the survivor to make an application for the month or months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(5.3): the Minister must notify the survivor in writing that an application is required` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` `the Minister requires the survivor to make an application for the month or months` MEANS
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` AND `the Minister requires the survivor to make an application for the month or months`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(5.3) "not later than fifteen days before" (src:591)
GIVEN `the first of the months for which the Minister requires an application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(5.3): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the months for which the Minister requires an application` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in days` 15) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` `the first of the months for which the Minister requires an application`)

-- (6) "An allowance may be paid under this section commencing with the month following the month in which the
-- applicant becomes a survivor or attains sixty years of age, whichever is later."
-- src:593 | (6) An allowance may be paid under this section commencing with the month following the month in which the applicant becomes a survivor or attains sixty years of age, whichever is later.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(6) (src:593)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(6): the first month for which an allowance may be paid` month facts MEANS
    `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` later
    WHERE
        sixty MEANS `the month in which a person born on` (facts's `the person's date of birth`) `attains the age of` 60
        survivor MEANS facts's `the month in which the person became a survivor`
        later MEANS IF `the first day of the month containing` sixty GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` survivor THEN sixty ELSE survivor

-- (7) "Notwithstanding subsections (6) and 23(2), no allowance may be paid under this section for any month prior to
-- September, 1985."
-- src:595 | (7) Notwithstanding subsections (6) and 23(2), no allowance may be paid under this section for any month prior to September, 1985.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(7) (src:595)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(7): the month is before September 1985` month MEANS
    `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN (YMD 1985 9 1)

-- (7.1) "In the case of a survivor who was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of this subsection
-- ("widow" having in this subsection the meaning that it had immediately before that coming into force), (a) no
-- allowance may be paid under this section unless the survivor became a survivor on or after January 1, 1998; and (b)
-- no allowance may be paid under this section for any month before the month in which this subsection comes into
-- force." The text gives no date of the coming into force: it is an input.
-- src:597 | (7.1) In the case of a survivor who was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of this subsection (“widow” having in this subsection the meaning that it had immediately before that coming into force),
-- src:598 | (a) no allowance may be paid under this section unless the survivor became a survivor on or after January 1, 1998; and
-- src:599 | (b) no allowance may be paid under this section for any month before the month in which this subsection comes into force.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(7.1) (src:597-599)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(7.1): a limitation for a survivor who was not a widow bars payment for the month` month facts MEANS
        facts's `the person was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1)`
    AND (   facts's `the day on which the person became a survivor` LESS THAN (YMD 1998 1 1)
         OR `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` (facts's `the month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force`))

-- (8) "An allowance under this section ceases to be payable on the expiration of the month in which the survivor in
-- respect of whom it is paid dies, attains sixty-five years of age or ceases to be a survivor." The age is dealt with
-- by (1)(a) (fork F-AGE-1); the death, and the day the person ceases to be a survivor, are facts.
-- src:601 | (8) An allowance under this section ceases to be payable on the expiration of the month in which the survivor in respect of whom it is paid dies, attains sixty-five years of age or ceases to be a survivor.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(8) (src:601)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the month in which the survivor dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which the survivor ceases to be a survivor` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(8): the allowance is still payable for the month` month `the month in which the survivor dies` `the month in which the survivor ceases to be a survivor` MEANS
        notYet `the month in which the survivor dies`
    AND notYet `the month in which the survivor ceases to be a survivor`
    WHERE
        notYet MEANS
            GIVEN when IS A MAYBE DATE
            YIELD CONSIDER when
                  WHEN JUST m THEN `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` m
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- (9)(a) "any month more than 11 months before the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have
-- been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived, as the case may be"
-- src:604 | (a) any month more than 11 months before the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived, as the case may be;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9)(a) (src:604)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9)(a): the month is more than eleven months before the month of the application` month facts MEANS
    `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 11) `months after the month containing` (facts's `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived`)

-- (9)(b) "any month throughout which the survivor is absent from Canada, having absented themself from Canada either
-- before or after becoming entitled to an allowance under this Part and having remained out of Canada before that
-- month for six consecutive months, exclusive of the month in which they left Canada"
-- src:605 | (b) any month throughout which the survivor is absent from Canada, having absented themself from Canada either before or after becoming entitled to an allowance under this Part and having remained out of Canada before that month for six consecutive months, exclusive of the month in which they left Canada; or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9)(b) (src:605)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9)(b): the survivor has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` month facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month`
    AND facts's `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving`
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person left Canada`
        WHEN JUST left THEN `the number of months from the month containing` left `to the month containing` month AT LEAST 7
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (9)(c) "any month during which the survivor is a person in respect of whom an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect as
-- provided under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act"; (9.1) "does not apply to a survivor (a) who was
-- qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which this paragraph comes into force, whether or
-- not they had applied for it; or (b) if an event as provided by the regulations has occurred."
-- src:606 | (c) any month during which the survivor is a person in respect of whom an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect as provided under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act; or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9)(c) (src:606)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9)(c): an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the survivor` facts MEANS
    facts's `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person`

-- src:611 | (9.1) Paragraph (9)(c) does not apply to a survivor
-- src:612 | (a) who was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which this paragraph comes into force, whether or not they had applied for it; or
-- src:613 | (b) if an event as provided by the regulations has occurred.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9.1) (src:611-613)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9.1): paragraph 21(9)(c) does not apply` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force`
    OR  facts's `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred`

-- (9)(d) "any period of incarceration - exclusive of the first month of that period - during which the survivor is
-- subject to a sentence of imprisonment (i) that is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of any Act of Parliament,
-- or (ii) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and
-- Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement
-- under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act."
-- src:607 | (d) any period of incarceration — exclusive of the first month of that period — during which the survivor is subject to a sentence of imprisonment
-- src:608 | (i) that is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of any Act of Parliament, or
-- src:609 | (ii) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9)(d) sentence (src:607-609)
GIVEN sentence IS A `Sentence of imprisonment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9)(d): the sentence of imprisonment is one described in the paragraph` sentence MEANS
        sentence's `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`
    OR (    sentence's `length in days` GREATER THAN 90
        AND sentence's `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
        AND sentence's `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`)

-- src:607 | (d) any period of incarceration — exclusive of the first month of that period — during which the survivor is subject to a sentence of imprisonment
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9)(d) (src:607)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9)(d): the month is in a period of incarceration, exclusive of the first month` month facts MEANS
        CONSIDER facts's `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to`
        WHEN JUST sentence THEN `s 21(9)(d): the sentence of imprisonment is one described in the paragraph` sentence
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the first day of the period of incarceration`
        WHEN JUST start THEN `the first day of the month containing` month GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` start
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person is released`
        WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` released
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- (9.2) "Payment of an allowance suspended by virtue of paragraph (9)(d) shall resume in respect of the month in which
-- the survivor is released but only if they (a) have notified the Minister in writing before or after their release;
-- and (b) continue to be eligible for an allowance."
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9.2) (src:615)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9.2): the month is the month of release` month facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person is released`
    WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month EQUALS `the first day of the month containing` released
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- src:615 | (9.2) Payment of an allowance suspended by virtue of paragraph (9)(d) shall resume in respect of the month in which the survivor is released but only if they
-- src:616 | (a) have notified the Minister in writing before or after their release; and
-- src:617 | (b) continue to be eligible for an allowance.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9.2) (src:615-617)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
      `the survivor continues to be eligible for an allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9.2): payment resumes in respect of the month of release` month facts `the survivor continues to be eligible for an allowance` MEANS
        `s 21(9.2): the month is the month of release` month facts
    AND facts's `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release`
    AND `the survivor continues to be eligible for an allowance`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9.2)(a) (src:616)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9.2): the month of release does not hold back payment` month facts MEANS
    NOT (`s 21(9.2): the month is the month of release` month facts AND NOT facts's `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release`)

-- (9) The limitations together, with the exception of (9.1).
-- src:603 | (9) No allowance may be paid under this section to a survivor pursuant to an application therefor for
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(9) (src:603)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(9): a limitation bars payment of an allowance for the month` month facts MEANS
        `s 21(9)(a): the month is more than eleven months before the month of the application` month facts
    OR `s 21(9)(b): the survivor has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` month facts
    OR (`s 21(9)(c): an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the survivor` facts AND NOT `s 21(9.1): paragraph 21(9)(c) does not apply` facts)
    OR `s 21(9)(d): the month is in a period of incarceration, exclusive of the first month` month facts

-- (1) to (9) together: an allowance may be paid under section 21 for the month. Section 21.1 is dealt with below.
-- src:573 | 21 (1) Subject to this Act and the regulations, for each month in any payment period, an allowance may be paid to a survivor who
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(1) lead-in (src:573)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21: an allowance may be paid to the survivor for the month` month facts MEANS
        `s 21(1): the person is a survivor` facts
    AND `s 21(1)(a): the survivor is at least sixty and under sixty-five` month facts
    AND `s 21(1)(b): the survivor has the required residence in Canada` facts
    AND `s 21(2): the survivor's residence in Canada is or was legal` facts
    AND `s 21(4): the requirement for an application and approval is met for the payment period` facts
    AND `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST `s 21(6): the first month for which an allowance may be paid` month facts
    AND NOT `s 21(7): the month is before September 1985` month
    AND NOT `s 21(7.1): a limitation for a survivor who was not a widow bars payment for the month` month facts
    AND `s 21(8): the allowance is still payable for the month` month (facts's `the month in which the person dies`) NOTHING
    AND NOT `s 21(9): a limitation bars payment of an allowance for the month` month facts
    AND `s 21(9.2): the month of release does not hold back payment` month facts

-- (10) "The amount of the allowance that may be paid under this section to a survivor shall be determined in
-- accordance with subsection 22(4)." (11) "Where subsection (5) applies, subsection (10) also applies in respect of
-- months in the payment period in respect of which the joint application was made and that are after the
-- pensioner's death."
-- src:619 | (10) The amount of the allowance that may be paid under this section to a survivor shall be determined in accordance with subsection 22(4).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(10) (src:619)
GIVEN `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement equivalent for the survivor in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(10): the amount of the allowance` `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` `the supplement equivalent for the survivor in respect of the month` `the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month` `the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period` MEANS
    `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` `the supplement equivalent for the survivor in respect of the month` `the survivor's special qualifying factor for the month` `the monthly income of the survivor in the current payment period`

-- src:621 | (11) Where subsection (5) applies, subsection (10) also applies in respect of months in the payment period in respect of which the joint application was made and that are after the pensioner’s death.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(11) (src:621)
GIVEN `subsection 21(5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is in the payment period in respect of which the joint application was made and is after the pensioner's death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(11): subsection 21(10) also applies in respect of the month` `subsection 21(5) applies` `the month is in the payment period in respect of which the joint application was made and is after the pensioner's death` MEANS
    `subsection 21(5) applies` AND `the month is in the payment period in respect of which the joint application was made and is after the pensioner's death`

-- (12) "A person's eligibility for an allowance under this section in respect of a deceased spouse or common-law partner is not
-- affected by the eligibility of another person for an allowance under this section in respect of that deceased spouse or
-- common-law partner." The rule takes the other person's eligibility as an input and gives the same answer as the rule for the
-- person alone, whatever it is.
-- src:623 | (12) A person’s eligibility for an allowance under this section in respect of a deceased spouse or common-law partner is not affected by the eligibility of another person for an allowance under this section in respect of that deceased spouse or common-law partner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21(12) (src:623)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month`
      `another person is eligible for an allowance in respect of the same deceased spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(12): an allowance may be paid to the survivor for the month, whether or not another person is eligible` month facts `another person is eligible for an allowance in respect of the same deceased spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    `s 21: an allowance may be paid to the survivor for the month` month facts

§§ `Allowance not payable, section 21.1`

-- 21.1(1) "Despite section 21, an allowance under that section is not payable to an individual who otherwise would
-- have been entitled to receive such an allowance as a result of the death of their spouse or common-law partner if
-- the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or
-- manslaughter of that spouse or common-law partner." (3) "If an individual has been convicted by a court outside
-- Canada in respect of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second
-- degree murder or manslaughter, the Minister may deem that conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree
-- murder or manslaughter for the purposes of this section." (8) "This section does not apply to an individual who is
-- convicted of manslaughter if the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under
-- paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code." (2) once the conviction is reversed, the charges withdrawn or the
-- proceedings stayed and not recommenced in time, and all rights of appeal are exhausted, subsection (1) is treated as
-- never having applied.
DECLARE `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction` HAS
    `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has deemed the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conviction is for manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Criminal Code section 731(1)(a) (no piece; a plain input)
    `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:638 | Exception — probation order
-- src:639 | (8) This section does not apply to an individual who is convicted of manslaughter if the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21.1(8) (src:638-639)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(8): section 21.1 does not apply to the individual` conviction MEANS
        conviction's `the conviction is for manslaughter`
    AND conviction's `the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code`

-- src:628 | Conviction outside Canada
-- src:629 | (3) If an individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada in respect of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter, the Minister may deem that conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter for the purposes of this section.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21.1(3) (src:628-629)
GIVEN `the individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada in respect of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(3): the Minister may deem the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` `the individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada in respect of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter` MEANS
    `the individual has been convicted by a court outside Canada in respect of an offence that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter`

-- src:626 | Conviction reversed
-- src:627 | (2) If the Minister is informed and satisfied that an individual’s conviction for first or second degree murder or manslaughter of their spouse or common-law partner has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period and that all rights of appeal have been exhausted, the individual’s entitlement to the allowance to which they would otherwise have been entitled under section 21 becomes payable in accordance with that section as if subsection (1) had never applied and any amount recovered from the person shall be repaid.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21.1(2) (src:626-627)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(2): the individual's entitlement becomes payable as if subsection 21.1(1) had never applied` conviction MEANS
        conviction's `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period`
    AND conviction's `all rights of appeal have been exhausted`

-- src:625 | 21.1 (1) Despite section 21, an allowance under that section is not payable to an individual who otherwise would have been entitled to receive such an allowance as a result of the death of their spouse or common-law partner if the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of that spouse or common-law partner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21.1(1) (src:625)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` conviction MEANS
        conviction's `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the spouse or common-law partner`
    AND ((NOT conviction's `the conviction is by a court outside Canada`) OR conviction's `the Minister has deemed the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter`)
    AND NOT `s 21.1(2): the individual's entitlement becomes payable as if subsection 21.1(1) had never applied` conviction
    AND NOT `s 21.1(8): section 21.1 does not apply to the individual` conviction

-- (4) "A person who has received an allowance referred to in this section and in respect of whom the Minister is
-- subsequently informed and satisfied that he or she has been convicted [...] shall be deemed not to have been
-- entitled to receive such an allowance, which shall constitute a debt due to Her Majesty under section 37 and the
-- Minister shall recover those amounts, including any amounts paid before the date of the individual's conviction."
-- src:631 | (4) A person who has received an allowance referred to in this section and in respect of whom the Minister is subsequently informed and satisfied that he or she has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of their spouse or common-law partner whose death would otherwise have resulted in the individual having been entitled to that allowance shall be deemed not to have been entitled to receive such an allowance, which shall constitute a debt due to Her Majesty under section 37 and the Minister shall recover those amounts, including any amounts paid before the date of the individual’s conviction.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21.1(4) (src:631)
GIVEN `the person has received an allowance referred to in this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      conviction IS A `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(4): the person is deemed not to have been entitled and the amounts are a debt that the Minister must recover` `the person has received an allowance referred to in this section` conviction MEANS     -- out of range: section 37 (piece oa1)
    `the person has received an allowance referred to in this section` AND `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` conviction

-- (2) "[...] and any amount recovered from the person shall be repaid."
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 21.1(2) "any amount recovered from the person shall be repaid" (src:627)
GIVEN `an amount has been recovered from the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      conviction IS A `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(2): the Minister must repay any amount recovered from the person` `an amount has been recovered from the person` conviction MEANS
    `an amount has been recovered from the person` AND `s 21.1(2): the individual's entitlement becomes payable as if subsection 21.1(1) had never applied` conviction
